Summary: Don't let the main thread and a GL thread change an OpenGL context's view at once
Category: graphics
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
  Note: written for wine-mac-builds
Upstream: no
Why: A WineOpenGLContext's view, latent view and update flags are changed
 by the GL threads (macdrv_make_context_current, macdrv_update_opengl_context)
 and, for contexts added while their view wasn't drawable, by the main thread
 in the content view's viewWillDraw, which calls
 macdrv_update_opengl_context. Nothing serialises the two. Both can read the
 same old view or latent view and release it, and the view is then released
 once too often. Add one recursive lock around those changes. A GL thread can
 hold it while it waits for the main thread (OnMainThread), so viewWillDraw
 only tries the lock. If it's busy, the context stays pending and the view
 asks to be drawn again.
 It needs a GL context made current on a view that isn't drawable yet,
 which Wine 11's framebuffer GL surfaces (EmulateModeset) cause when two
 threads draw to one window: each gets its own surface and view.
 Upstream winemac has the same code in 10.0 and 11.x.
 Found while chasing a crash at objc_release+34 in Nancy Drew games
 ("Pattern A"), but it isn't that crash: an instrumented build logged no
 pending-context update and no overlap in any of the games' launches,
 crashed or not.
Programs: Nancy Drew games (Shadow Ranch, Old Clock, Crystal Skull, Castle
 Malloy): a crash at objc_release+34 ("Pattern A") led to this patch, but
 the race it fixes isn't shown to be that crash
Evidence: A winemac instrumented to count threads inside each context's
 functions reported about 40 overlaps in 15 s of a stress program (one
 context per render thread, two render threads switching between two
 windows while the main thread hides and shows them, EmulateModeset on).
 All were viewWillDraw's update on the main thread while a GL thread was
 inside. There were none with this patch. The stress program doesn't
 crash, as the double release needs a narrower interleaving, so there is
 no regression test.
Status: 11.22: built in macfixes-11.22-build7 (2026-11-17); the regression suite passes
 on it (screen tests skipped on that run; they passed on a build6 tree with
 this winemac.so). Second Chance's four Pattern A games ran 32 launches without
 a crash on that tree, against 2 in 8 on build6, though nothing shows why.
 On meeka (macOS 26.7), White Wolf launched 10 of 10 times over 5 runs on
 build7 without hanging, and Bioscopia passed (launch 4m 22s, against
 5m 09s on build6).
 On kiya (macOS 15.6.1), all 33 Nancy Drew games passed on build7 (about
 54 launches), with no c0000005, including the six that had crashed on
 earlier builds. With the 32 launches above, that's no Pattern A crash in
 about 86 launches with 0060, though it's still not shown why.
 2026-11-18: Pattern A's cause was found and is fixed by 0066 (a context
 released on the main thread after a GL thread freed it); it still
 happened with this patch (d3d8-up-draw-speed, 4 of 115 runs on build12).
 11.21: 2026-11-17: built in macfixes-11.21-build8. The same change as
 11.22's. The regression suite passes on it on macOS 15.6.1 (42 passed; the
 two fullscreen screen tests skipped, and exe-base-taken, which needs
 11.22). No games run on it yet.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
index 5488840..5bb2850 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
@@ -26,6 +26,16 @@
 #include "cocoa_app.h"
 #include "cocoa_event.h"
 
+#include <pthread.h>
+
+/* Held while a context's view, latent view and update flags change. The
+ * GL threads change them in macdrv_make_context_current() and
+ * macdrv_update_opengl_context(), and the main thread in the content view's
+ * viewWillDraw. Without it both could swap the same view at once and release
+ * it twice. A GL thread can hold it while it waits for the main thread, so
+ * the main thread only ever tries to take it. */
+static pthread_mutex_t context_mutex = PTHREAD_RECURSIVE_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
+
 #pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wdeclaration-after-statement"
 
 
@@ -218,7 +228,9 @@ void macdrv_dispose_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context)
 {
 @autoreleasepool
 {
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&context_mutex);
     [context removeFromViews:YES];
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&context_mutex);
     [context release];
 }
 }
@@ -230,6 +242,7 @@ void macdrv_make_context_current(WineOpenGLContext *context, WineContentView *vi
 {
 @autoreleasepool
 {
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&context_mutex);
     if (context && view)
     {
         if (view == (WineContentView *)[context view] || view == (WineContentView *)[context latentView])
@@ -278,6 +291,7 @@ void macdrv_make_context_current(WineOpenGLContext *context, WineContentView *vi
         if (context)
             [context removeFromViews:YES];
     }
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&context_mutex);
 }
 }
 
@@ -288,6 +302,7 @@ void macdrv_update_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context)
 {
 @autoreleasepool
 {
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&context_mutex);
     if (context.needsUpdate)
     {
         BOOL reattach = context.needsReattach;
@@ -321,7 +336,23 @@ void macdrv_update_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context)
             [context resetSurfaceIfBackingSizeChanged];
         }
     }
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&context_mutex);
+}
 }
+
+/***********************************************************************
+ *              macdrv_try_update_opengl_context
+ *
+ * For the main thread: updates the context unless a GL thread is changing
+ * it, and returns whether it did.
+ */
+int macdrv_try_update_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context)
+{
+    if (pthread_mutex_trylock(&context_mutex)) return 0;
+    context.needsUpdate = TRUE;
+    macdrv_update_opengl_context(context);
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&context_mutex);
+    return 1;
 }
 
 /***********************************************************************
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
index 38b12b0..9042a24 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -466,13 +466,20 @@ - (void) viewWillDraw
     {
         [super viewWillDraw];
 
-        for (WineOpenGLContext* context in pendingGlContexts)
+        for (WineOpenGLContext* context in [[pendingGlContexts copy] autorelease])
         {
-            context.needsUpdate = TRUE;
-            macdrv_update_opengl_context(context);
+            /* A GL thread is changing it; leave it pending for the next draw. */
+            if (!macdrv_try_update_opengl_context(context))
+                continue;
+            [glContexts addObject:context];
+            [pendingGlContexts removeObjectIdenticalTo:context];
+        }
+        if ([pendingGlContexts count])
+        {
+            dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{
+                [self setNeedsDisplay:YES];
+            });
         }
-        [glContexts addObjectsFromArray:pendingGlContexts];
-        [pendingGlContexts removeAllObjects];
     }
 
     - (void) addGLContext:(WineOpenGLContext*)context
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_cocoa.h b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_cocoa.h
index c7950d9..88fe8b8 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_cocoa.h
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_cocoa.h
@@ -551,6 +551,7 @@ extern WineOpenGLContext *macdrv_create_opengl_context(void* cglctx);
 extern void macdrv_dispose_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context);
 extern void macdrv_make_context_current(WineOpenGLContext *context, WineContentView *view, CGRect r);
 extern void macdrv_update_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context);
+extern int macdrv_try_update_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context);
 extern void macdrv_flush_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context);
 
 
